# UITK design mirror (UX sandbox)

Authority: [docs/04-dev/uitk-design-mirror.md](../../docs/04-dev/uitk-design-mirror.md). Tracking: [griddungeon-game#422](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/issues/422).

## Purpose

UI/UX edits **placeholder-filled mirror UXML/USS** in Unity UI Builder under `Assets/UI/Editor/DesignMirror/`. Devs/agents promote layout and USS to production bindables in `Assets/UI/Screens/` via **sync-uitk-design-mirror** skill.

**One-way flow:** mirror → production. Production shells keep empty runtime hosts and stable `name` hooks.

## Who edits what

| Role | Path | Tool |
|------|------|------|
| UI/UX | `Assets/UI/Editor/DesignMirror/**` | Unity UI Builder |
| Dev/agent sync | `Assets/UI/Screens/**` (shell + USS) | **sync-uitk-design-mirror** |
| Dev/agent bootstrap | `Assets/UI/Editor/DesignMirror/**` | **create-uitk-design-mirror** |

**Never** ask UX to open production `Screens/` UXML or USS in UI Builder (USS auto-reorder risk).

## Build exclusion

Mirror assets live in Unity `Editor` folder — excluded from player builds. **No new asmdef.** No Runtime references to mirror assets from presenters.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Read `Assets/UI/Editor/DesignMirror/mirror-manifest.yaml` before create/sync
- [ ] Create/refresh mirror only with **create-uitk-design-mirror**
- [ ] Promote UX edits only with **sync-uitk-design-mirror**
- [ ] Strip `stripHosts` children when syncing to production shell
- [ ] Prettier on touched `.uxml` / `.uss` before handoff
- [ ] No `phase`, `MVP`, `mvp`, or `PoC` in `Assets/**` ([default-release-scope-language.mdc](default-release-scope-language.mdc))

## Related skills

- **create-uitk-design-mirror** — bootstrap mirror + fixture placeholders
- **sync-uitk-design-mirror** — promote to production
- **visualize-uitk-uxml** — production tree before editing
- **prettier-uitk-format** — format changed UITK assets
